# React Composition Patterns

When designing or refactoring React component APIs, first use:

`~/.cursor/skills/composition-patterns/SKILL.md`

Apply relevant `rules/` guidance with priority on:
- Avoid boolean-prop proliferation for behavior modes.
- Prefer composition and compound components over monolithic prop APIs.
- Lift shared state into provider boundaries when siblings need coordination.
- Keep state interfaces generic and decoupled from implementation details.
- Prefer explicit variant components and `children` composition over renderX props.

If React 19 APIs are in scope, apply only React 19-specific rules.

When reporting changes, mention which composition rules were applied.
